      "locale": "en",
      "runtime_text": "In fish smoking, drying removes some water, smoke deposits compounds on the product, and heat acts differently in hot and cold processes; salt, when used, lowers available water. The preservative effect depends on the actual combination of these factors, not one sign. This establishes no recipe, duration, temperature, stock, safety, or batch outcome.",
